From 0364c8ebea8be81332f48e8bd3da907bc45dae1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:59:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/17] Safarium: hide settings and menu items that need Google
 or Chrome's UI

Link menu: no "Open Link in Split View" (no split view) or "Add Link to
Reading List" (nowhere to read it).

Settings: hide Autofill with AI categories (identity docs, travel),
loyalty cards, shopping, Gemini suggestions, Wallet / Google Account links,
card benefits and the Wallet note (Google account services); Safe Browsing
enhanced protection, password leak check and the Advanced Protection link
(need Google sign-in / API keys); Live Translate and AXTree fixing (Google
servers); copy confirmations (Chrome toasts, which Safarium's window has
no host for). History: no synced-tabs page or sync promo. Password
Manager: no automated password change (needs sign-in).

Elements stay in the templates where WebUI lint requires them, hidden in
Safarium builds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
